# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 6. GENERATED CONTEXT GRAPH (graphify)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# graphify's output dir (graph.json + graph.html + AST cache + manifest) is a
# rebuildable PROJECTION — regenerate with scripts/graphify-build.ps1, never
# hand-edit (two-tier-truth rule). Gitignored until a path-normalizer makes
# graph.json diff cleanly cross-machine; see docs/graph/README.md + memory 0008.
graphify-out/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 7. BRAIN-INGEST LOCAL CORPUS CACHE
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The paper manifest (papers.jsonl), usage.json, and browser-captured html are
# now a LOCAL CACHE — R2 is the canonical metadata + binary store (manifest/
# papers.jsonl + meta/<uid>.json + pdf|jats|text). See BRAIN-INGESTION-DESIGN §1/§6.
data/corpus/

# Provider acceptance artifacts/state are task-scoped and rebuildable. Keep this
# exact directory ignored so a completed leg cannot dirty the reviewed Git head.
data/brain-ingest/live-acceptance/

# llm-router runtime state: budget ledger + local-agent mailbox (request/response
# audit files). Rebuildable/ephemeral run state, never truth — see
# tools/llm-router/README.md.
data/llm-router/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 8. MODEL-TRAINING (Python workspace) — model-training/, see AGENTS.md §1/§4
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Root-level staging area for complete model bundles awaiting upload to
# approved external object storage (for example, private Cloudflare R2).
/model/

# Every pattern below is anchored to /model-training/: it is the repo's one
# isolated Python workspace, and anchoring keeps an ML-specific pattern (e.g.
# *.onnx, *.bin) from ever matching an unrelated path elsewhere in the tree —
# a past incident here was caused by a non-anchored pattern matching more
# than intended, so anchoring is deliberate, not an oversight (see the
# .open-next/ note in §3 for the opposite, intentionally-non-anchored case).

# Workspace-local virtualenvs (root env/venv/.venv/ above already matches
# these non-anchored; kept explicit here so the workspace section is
# self-describing on its own).
/model-training/.venv/
/model-training/venv/

# Python tool caches: never useful to commit, always regenerable from source.
/model-training/**/__pycache__/
/model-training/**/*.py[cod]
/model-training/.mypy_cache/
/model-training/.ruff_cache/
/model-training/.pytest_cache/

# Scratch experiment code. Ignored WHOLESALE, extensions included, because the
# risk here is the .py itself rather than a dataset: these scripts are written
# against licence-restricted corpora (SciFact is CC BY-NC) and quote them in
# fixtures and docstrings, so the source file carries the licence problem even
# when no corpus file sits beside it. The extension rules below deliberately do
# not match a bare .py, which is exactly how `git add -A` swept four of these
# into PR #311 — caught only as a model-training lint failure, not as a licence
# gate. Promised on #311 and landed here; see also #277 for the licence scope.
/model-training/experiments/*
!/model-training/experiments/2026-07-31-disagreement-pilot/

# Raw datasets. Every training plan's licence gate treats PMIDs/labels/
# manifests as the committed artifact and the underlying corpus text/files
# as never-committed — see docs/temp/model-training/*-training-plan.md.
/model-training/**/data/
/model-training/**/datasets/
/model-training/**/raw/

# Corpus/label files by extension, anywhere in the workspace — not only under
# data|datasets|raw. A downloaded corpus lands wherever the script's cwd was,
# and "I put it in the wrong folder" must not be the difference between
# committing MEDLINE text and not. The two negations below are the committed
# dependency manifests (D4), which are deliberately tracked.
/model-training/**/*.jsonl
/model-training/**/*.ndjson
/model-training/**/*.csv
/model-training/**/*.tsv
/model-training/**/*.txt
/model-training/**/*.xml
/model-training/**/*.xml.gz
/model-training/**/*.gz
/model-training/**/*.zip
/model-training/**/*.parquet
!/model-training/constraints.txt
!/model-training/**/requirements*.txt

# Disagreement-pilot evidence (issue #277). Zebra v1 / Viceroy v0 vs Claude
# Haiku 4.5 on real ingested papers — cited by the hackathon submission, so the
# numbers must be independently checkable rather than asserted.
#
# Named ONE BY ONE, following the #266 convention immediately below: the data
# dir is re-included so git descends into it, then re-excluded wholesale, then
# each reviewed artifact is named. A directory-wide negation would commit any
# corpus file later dropped in that folder — the exact accident the extension
# rules above exist to prevent.
#
# Only DERIVED artifacts are named. The pilot's *-inputs.jsonl, *-clean.jsonl
# and ADJUDICATE-*.tsv carry VERBATIM third-party paper text and are therefore
# NOT named, so they stay ignored by the rules above. `row_id` values are DOIs,
# so anyone can re-fetch the sources: referenced, never redistributed.
!/model-training/experiments/2026-07-31-disagreement-pilot/data/
/model-training/experiments/2026-07-31-disagreement-pilot/data/*
!/model-training/experiments/2026-07-31-disagreement-pilot/data/zebra-pilot-preds.jsonl
!/model-training/experiments/2026-07-31-disagreement-pilot/data/viceroy-pilot-preds.jsonl
!/model-training/experiments/2026-07-31-disagreement-pilot/data/zebra-key.json
!/model-training/experiments/2026-07-31-disagreement-pilot/data/viceroy-key.json
!/model-training/experiments/2026-07-31-disagreement-pilot/data/haiku-labels.tsv
!/model-training/experiments/2026-07-31-disagreement-pilot/data/haiku-zebra-labels.tsv

# Frozen public inference-input manifests (issue #266). These are named ONE BY
# ONE, not as a `inference-manifests/*.jsonl` glob, and that is deliberate: a
# directory-wide negation would mean anyone who dropped a downloaded corpus in
# that folder would commit it, which is precisely the accident the extension
# rules above exist to prevent. A named negation costs one line per reviewed
# fixture and cannot be triggered by accident.
#
# Anything added here must be public/frozen, contain no corpus text under a
# restrictive licence, and no product or user data.
!/model-training/inference-manifests/zebra-smoke-v1.jsonl
!/model-training/inference-manifests/viceroy-smoke-v0.jsonl

# Checkpoints, exported weights, and predictions. No training or export has
# been run in this code-build (see docs/temp/model-training/human-gates.md);
# this also fails closed against ever committing one later.
/model-training/**/*.safetensors
/model-training/**/*.ckpt
/model-training/**/*.bin
/model-training/**/*.pt
/model-training/**/*.pth
/model-training/**/*.onnx
/model-training/**/*.h5
/model-training/**/*.hdf5
/model-training/**/*.gguf
/model-training/**/*.ggml
/model-training/**/*.tflite
/model-training/**/*.pb
/model-training/**/*.msgpack
/model-training/**/*.npy
/model-training/**/*.npz
/model-training/**/*.pkl
/model-training/**/*.pickle
/model-training/**/*.joblib
/model-training/**/*.model
/model-training/**/*.vocab
/model-training/**/checkpoints/
/model-training/**/predictions/

# Experiment trackers and other local run artifacts.
/model-training/**/mlruns/
/model-training/**/wandb/
/model-training/**/.neptune/
/model-training/**/runs/
/model-training/**/outputs/
